# Cobalt Warrens: an interconnected-map exploration platformer invented as a genre example. No
# game's names, data or logic. A salvager lands at an abandoned mining colony and explores one
# large map in five zones, joined both ways; movement gear opens new parts of it, so the player
# keeps coming back to rooms seen earlier. Each zone is its own file, as a world this size
# would be split.
world cobalt_warrens "Cobalt Warrens" version 1
use items
use logic
use zones/surface
use zones/mines
use zones/foundry
use zones/aqueduct
use zones/reactor
start landing_pad

# How much the logic trusts the player's movement skill. `basic` and `advanced` count known
# tricks (a dash off a wall, a climb without the gloves) as ways through.
option tricks: choice(none, basic, advanced) = none
# How many of the two bosses must be beaten before the reactor door takes the keycard.
option bosses_needed: range 0..2 = 2
# Start with the thruster, for shorter seeds.
option start_thruster: toggle = off

start_item thruster when opt.start_thruster

goal reactor_shut_down
